an Ramezani","email":"hasan.r67@gmail.com","date":"2026-10-28T09:53:21Z"},"message":"Extend tests for nested container dict value types\n\nMove the regression test next to the other nested dict env tests and\ncover more shapes from #1107: Annotated value types, Optional dicts,\ndicts inside models (and models inside dicts), and dict keys that\nmatch a field name of the dict's value model.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PRaoYMkPxtZ35KHCmqCYHf","tree":{"sha":"4765e3b59f620b5094a7cc977cd1b139247c3fb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/git/trees/4765e3b59f620b5094a7cc977cd1b139247c3fb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/git/commits/74c01ae3e84f9c8f2b04ec269e67813abd96cf9a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commits/74c01ae3e84f9c8f2b04ec269e67813abd96cf9a","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/74c01ae3e84f9c8f2b04ec269e67813abd96cf9a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commits/74c01ae3e84f9c8f2b04ec269e67813abd96cf9a/comments","author":{"login":"hramezani","id":3122442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMjI0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3122442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani","html_url":"https://github.com/hramezani","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"hramezani","id":3122442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMjI0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3122442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani","html_url":"https://github.com/hramezani","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hramezani/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"36f3d9f481df0310ee75370c06017d8825ed5447","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commits/36f3d9f481df0310ee75370c06017d8825ed5447","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/36f3d9f481df0310ee75370c06017d8825ed5447"}]}],"files":[{"sha":"78cb87aca4914db3f4c9051551a3507baa1b2f5d","filename":"tests/test_settings.py","status":"modified","additions":74,"deletions":18,"changes":92,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/blob/74c01ae3e84f9c8f2b04ec269e67813abd96cf9a/tests%2Ftest_settings.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/raw/74c01ae3e84f9c8f2b04ec269e67813abd96cf9a/tests%2Ftest_settings.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-settings/contents/tests%2Ftest_settings.py?ref=74c01ae3e84f9c8f2b04ec269e67813abd96cf9a","patch":"@@ -4437,6 +4437,80 @@ class Settings(BaseSettings):\n     assert s.model_dump() == {'nested_field': {'key': ['a', 'b']}}\n \n \n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    'value_type,value',\n+    [\n+        (list[dict[str, str]], [{'k': 'v'}]),\n+        (dict[str, list[str]], {'k': ['v']}),\n+        (dict[str, dict[str, int]], {'k': {'nested': 1}}),\n+        (list[list[dict[str, str]]], [[{'k': 'v'}]]),\n+        (Annotated[list[dict[str, str]], Field(min_length=1)], [{'k': 'v'}]),\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_env_nested_dict_nested_container_value_type(env, value_type, value):\n+    \"\"\"Regression test for https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/1107\"\"\"\n+\n+    class Settings(BaseSettings):\n+        nested_field: dict[str, value_type]\n+\n+        model_config = SettingsConfigDict(env_nested_delimiter='__')\n+\n+    env.set('nested_field__key', json.dumps(value))\n+    s = Settings()\n+    assert s.model_dump() == {'nested_field': {'key': value}}\n+\n+\n+class _DictOfListOfDicts(BaseModel):\n+    d: dict[str, list[dict[str, str]]] = {}\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n+    'annotation,env_name,expected',\n+    [\n+        (typing.Optional[dict[str, list[dict[str, str]]]], 'field__key', {'key': [{'k': 'v'}]}),  # noqa: UP045\n+        (dict[str, list[dict[str, str]]] | None, 'field__key', {'key': [{'k': 'v'}]}),\n+        (_DictOfListOfDicts, 'field__d__key', {'d': {'key': [{'k': 'v'}]}}),\n+        (dict[str, _DictOfListOfDicts], 'field__a__d__key', {'a': {'d': {'key': [{'k': 'v'}]}}}),\n+    ],\n+)\n+def test_env_nested_dict_nested_container_value_type_in_wrapper(env, annotation, env_name, expected):\n+    \"\"\"Regression test for https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/1107\"\"\"\n+\n+    class Settings(BaseSettings):\n+        field: annotation\n+\n+        model_config = SettingsConfigDict(env_nested_delimiter='__')\n+\n+    env.set(env_name, '[{\"k\": \"v\"}]')\n+    s = Settings()\n+    assert s.model_dump() == {'field': expected}\n+\n+\n+def test_env_nested_dict_model_value_key_matching_model_field(env):\n+    \"\"\"A dict key that matches a field name of the dict's value model is still a dict key.\"\"\"\n+\n+    class Value(BaseModel):\n+        name: str\n+        count: int = 0\n+\n+    class Settings(BaseSettings):\n+        values: dict[str, Value]\n+\n+        model_config = SettingsConfigDict(env_nested_delimiter='__')\n+\n+    env.set('values__name', '{\"name\": \"a\", \"count\": 1}')\n+    env.set('values__count', '{\"name\": \"b\", \"count\": 2}')\n+    env.set('values__other__name', 'c')\n+    s = Settings()\n+    assert s.model_dump() == {\n+        'values': {\n+            'name': {'name': 'a', 'count': 1},\n+            'count': {'name': 'b', 'count': 2},\n+            'other': {'name': 'c', 'count': 0},\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+\n ListOrStr = TypeAliasType('ListOrStr', list[str] | str)\n \n \n@@ -5763,21 +5837,3 @@ class Settings(BaseSettings):\n     messages = [r.getMessage() for r in caplog.records]\n     assert any(f'Loading secret file: {(tmp_path / \"name\").resolve()}' == m for m in messages)\n     assert any('Secret file not found, skipping' in m and 'missing' in m for m in messages)\n-\n-\n-@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n-    'value_type,value',\n-    [\n-        (list[dict[str, str]], [{'k': 'v'}]),\n-        (dict[str, list[str]], {'k': ['v']}),\n-        (dict[str, dict[str, int]], {'k': {'nested': 1}}),\n-        (list[list[dict[str, str]]], [[{'k': 'v'}]]),\n-    ],\n-)\n-def test_nested_dict_env_value_preserves_container_type(env, value_type, value):\n-    class Settings(BaseSettings):\n-        model_config = SettingsConfigDict(env_prefix='APP_', env_nested_delimiter='__')\n-        values: dict[str, value_type]\n-\n-    env.set('APP_VALUES__X', json.dumps(value))\n-    assert Settings().values == {'x': value}"}]}